WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:11.520
One of the most common questions you see in the&nbsp;
aiming community is how to fix shaky or jittery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:18.000
aim. In this video, we’ll cover 4 simple steps&nbsp;
you can try today to achieve silky smooth aim.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:24.640
Number 1 is to reduce friction. If the skin&nbsp;
of your hand, wrist or arm is catching on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:31.360
mousepad or desk there are a few things you can&nbsp;
try. Firstly, wash your hand/wrist and arm with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:36.720
soap and dry off, and repeat when things start to&nbsp;
feel like they’re slowing down or catching again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.760
If everything suddenly feels too fast&nbsp;
after this, you can skip the soap.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:48.000
Wearing a sports sleeve can also be very helpful&nbsp;
for reducing friction, although washing your hand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.720
and wrist is still a good idea. We have an arm&nbsp;
sleeve video in the description for more info.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.400
Your mousepad can also be the cause of&nbsp;
shaky aim, particularly if it’s old and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.880
worn out. Look into giving it a clean&nbsp;
or simply replacing it if possible.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:09.760
Number 2 is adjusting your mouse sensitivity.&nbsp;
Generally speaking, higher sensitivities are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:15.760
harder to play smoothly, while lower sensitivities&nbsp;
make it much easier. Even revered players like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:22.560
Overwatch’s Pine who plays on a very high&nbsp;
sensitivity of 18.5cm/360 has shaky aim.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.160
Playing on lower sens doesn’t mean you’ve suddenly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.920
solved this deficiency, but it can let&nbsp;
you avoid the problem all together.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:35.920
Number 3 is focusing on your target.&nbsp;
This one is huge, and if done correctly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:40.320
it will feel like this lightbulb moment&nbsp;
where everything just falls into place.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.640
There is a huge difference between looking&nbsp;
at a target, and focusing on a target.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.560
Take this ceiling fan for example. You can look&nbsp;
right at it and the blades are a blur. But if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:55.840
you focus on a blade you can track it spinning&nbsp;
around. This is the difference we are looking for.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.440
Just looking at your target means you are missing&nbsp;
out on loads of information about it’s speed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:06.480
trajectory and other visual cues. This makes&nbsp;
the movement of your opponents feel fast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.960
erratic and hard to follow, and as such&nbsp;
your aim will also be erratic and shaky.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:17.040
Focusing on your target will instantly make it&nbsp;
feel like it’s moving slower and more predictably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.840
and as such you can track it with calculated&nbsp;
aiming movements that are much smoother.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:27.040
Number 4 is through aim training. There&nbsp;
are many different ways to approach this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.200
so we will cover some simple first steps.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:35.680
Firstly, jump in KovaaKs and play Smoothness&nbsp;
Training 60. This is a simple scenario with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:40.400
a predetermined strafing pattern so you don’t&nbsp;
need to worry about reactivity or reaction time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.000
It will purely test your ability&nbsp;
to track the target horizontally.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.200
Don’t worry about the score too much, even&nbsp;
with shaky aim it can be perfectly tracked.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:54.800
So instead, do your best to track it smoothly,&nbsp;
and reflect on how shaky or smooth it feels.&nbsp;

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.960
To find more scenarios that can&nbsp;
aid in improving your smoothness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:02.560
navigate to online scenarios,&nbsp;
click advanced search,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:08.640
choose tracking and then smoothness. If you want&nbsp;
to be even more selective, simply type smooth or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:13.040
smoothness in the search bar to find scenarios&nbsp;
people have made specifically for this skill.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.320
And there we have it, 4 simple steps to&nbsp;
get rid of shaky aim. We hope you found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:22.800
this video helpful, let us know which tip&nbsp;
worked best for you in the comments below,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:31.840
subscribe for more content like this,&nbsp;
and we’ll catch you in the next one.

